 Understanding Privacy Settings on Social Media
Social media platforms offer extensive privacy settings, but many users never adjust them. 
Learning to use the internet responsibly means taking control of who can see your posts, your profile, 
and your personal information. Users should regularly review their privacy settings, limit the audience for their content, and be cautious about sharing location data or personal milestones.
Understanding that "public" means visible to anyone, including potential employers and scammers,
is essential for maintaining a healthy digital footprint.
